      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Bump post up. I am still waiting for very easy saving feature. We can save settings on avatars, but why nothing for camera pins?\n\nThis is not hard to program feature and it will make people happy. You did it already on avatars. And you can add button to erase camera pins.\n\nAnd another pins feature is full cycle. I can only cycle 1-2 or 2-3 but there is nothing for 1-2-3 cycle. Why is this not possible? It's so easy to make it possible. I don't like open camera pins again and click on it, but problem is also it change cycle mode again to 1-2 or 2-3. Make it full 1-2-3 and i am happy.\n\nIn camera we can simply see pin number, so it's no problem at all and it just make things faster and easier! Very good for streamers but maybe also for RP recorders.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-13T09:37:47.444Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's nice to make 3 different camera settings and store them in the pins.\nBut it's sad there is no feature to save pins settings for long time. I noticed there are some requests for 2 years, where people want save camera settings / positions.\nEspecially VRChat streamers have mostly fixed camera setups, and they must set it again and again when start VRChat up. Same for VRChat crash, setup again is really no fun.\nWhy is this simple feature never added to VRChat client? We have newer Menu UI, we have newer camera UI, and still, there is no save feature.\nI don't get it, dear VRChat developers. It's one of the long requested feature, and i am sure this is not hard to program it. It can just saved locally (or even nicer in cloud like avatars).\nTwo posts i found have this request:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/save-camera-pins\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/1140-camera-settings-reset-upon-relaunch-of-vrc-client\nSo yeah, i am not one here. Many (famous) VRChat streamers want save their fixed camera setup.\nIt's sounds not much, but i am streamer and i have always fixed setup.",
